# The signature says the log changes, as `&mut Log` or as `&RefCell<Log>`: each `note` takes the log as it was and
# makes it at its own moment, and inside it `push` makes the log's lines anew. A struct expression builds its struct,
# as a constructor does; `RefCell::new` is a library operation whose result `run` names, the cell that holds the Log.
# `run` counts the lines of both logs itself.
route journal.run
step run/Log()
step run/note
step run/note/push
step run/Log()#2
step run/note_shared

line entry > run call
line run/Log() > Log·log@run/Log() value
line Log·log@run/Log() > run/note/push value
line run/note/push > Log·log@run/note/push value
line Log·log@run/note/push > run/note value
line run/note > Log·log@run/note value
line run/note_shared > Log·shared@run/note_shared value
line Log·shared@run/note_shared > run value

home Log·log@run/Log() run
home Log·log@run/note/push run/note
home Log·log@run/note run
home Log·shared@run/note_shared run

side entry left

# A library operation whose result the body names (`let shared = RefCell::new(..)`), or that changes what a call gives
# (`log.borrow_mut().lines.push(..)`), is no step
known #125 step run/new
known #125 step run/note_shared/push
known #125 line run/Log()#2 > Log@run/Log()#2 value
known #125 line Log@run/Log()#2 > run/new value
known #125 line run/new > Log·shared@run/new value
known #125 line Log·shared@run/new > run/note_shared/push value
known #125 line run/note_shared/push > Log·log@run/note_shared/push value
known #125 line Log·log@run/note_shared/push > run/note_shared value
known #125 home Log@run/Log()#2 run
known #125 home Log·shared@run/new run
known #125 home Log·log@run/note_shared/push run/note_shared
known #125 extra line run/Log()#2 > Log·shared@run/Log()#2 value
known #125 extra line Log·shared@run/Log()#2 > run/note_shared value
known #125 extra home Log·shared@run/Log()#2 run

# `run` reads the lines of the log `note` changed
known #101 line Log·log@run/note > run value
